summary: Test RTC using hwclock
description: |
    rtc-hwclock Introduction
    ========================

    This is a simple test to test RTC functionality using the 'hwclock'
    utility from util-linux.
    The test will check whether setting a new time to the RTC works
    combining different cases, like Daylight Saving and UTC/localtime
    setting.
    It will restore the correct time at the end by using the internal Red
    Hat NTP server.
contact: Erico Nunes <ernunes@redhat.com>
test: ./runtest.sh
framework: beakerlib
require:
  - util-linux
# hwclock is not included in the util-linux build for s390x
adjust:
  - enable: false
    when: arch == s390x
duration: 1h
extra-summary: /kernel/misc/rtc-hwclock
extra-task: /kernel/misc/rtc-hwclock
